 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The gate turns on between 0.8 V and 2.8 V (1.4 V typical) at 250 µA drain current. On-resistance is guaranteed at two drive levels with 0.17 A flowing: 6.0 Ω max at VGS = 10 V and 10 Ω max at 4.5 V. In Figure 3 the typical value at 50 mA is about 3.3 Ω at 10 V and 3.7 Ω at 4.5 V, rising to about 4.7 Ω and 5.4 Ω at 0.5 A. The gate withstands ±20 V and leaks at most ±50 nA at that voltage."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Off state",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Breakdown is at least 100 V. With the gate at 0 V the drain leaks no more than 0.1 µA at 100 V and 0.01 µA at 20 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "On-resistance climbs about linearly with temperature in Figure 4, to roughly 1.5 times its 25 °C value at 100 °C and 1.9 times at 150 °C. In Figure 2 the 125 °C transfer curve starts conducting at a lower gate voltage than the 25 °C curve and the two cross near 3.6 V and 0.75 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Dissipation is rated 0.68 W, and the steady-state junction-to-ambient resistance is 417 °C/W. The junction and storage ranges are both -55 °C to +150 °C. Figure 7 scales its normalized transient curves by an RθJA of 104 °C/W."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The source-to-drain diode carries up to 0.34 A continuously and drops at most 1.3 V at 0.34 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Charge to bring the gate to 10 V against 30 V and 0.28 A is 1.4 nC typical, 2.0 nC max, with 0.15 nC gate-source and 0.2 nC gate-drain. Switched from a 50 Ω generator at VDD = 30 V, VGS = 10 V and 0.28 A, turn-on delay and rise are each 8.0 ns max, turn-off delay 13 ns max and fall 16 ns max."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "SOT-23 case; the moulding compound is rated UL 94V-0 for flammability, and the part is RoHS-compliant and halogen-free. Leads are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 Method 2026."
  }
